2026-09-09T13:31Z MinhHaDuong note Batch of decisions: fetch item titles (yes) and check `item.attachmentFilename` as an available identifier; redact the filepath from inspection-error's text (`classifyError` already does this by construction -- checked, not assumed, bootstrap.js:419-426, never reads `error.message`); failed-session and the unsupported-pack version split, both already folded in above; add a clarifying tooltip to both buttons; do not frame anything as a problem anywhere in this feature, only facts -- extended beyond the remedy sentences to every heading, subsection title and control label; do all necessary measurements rather than guess the remainder. A third derisking fork dispatched for the three still-unmeasured facts: attachmentFilename's real mechanism and coverage, the actual title-resolution cost across the affected population, and whether any class spans more than one library on real data.

